      "extract_value": "This section reports manipulation checks: ANOVAs showed the appearance article was perceived as more appearance-focused than the health article (F(1, 161) = 31.62, p < .001; health M = 3.33, SD = 0.81; appearance M = 4.05, SD = 0.82). The guilt manipulation increased immediate self-reported guilt (F(1, 161) = 13.02, p < .001; guilt M = 2.95, SD = 1.69; no guilt M = 2.02, SD = 1.58), while introjected regulation was unaffected by the manipulations.",
      "evidence_source": "\"Participants perceived the author in the appearance conditions as significantly more appearance-focused than the author in the health conditions F(1, 161) = 31.62, p < .001; health conditions: M = 3.33, SD = 0.81; appearance conditions: M = 4.05, SD = 0.82.\"; \"In the case of post-test guilt, a 2 \u00d7 2 ANOVA indicated that the guilt manipulation had a significant effect on participants' immediate emotional reports of guilt, F(1, 161) = 13.02, p < .001; guilt conditions: M = 2.95, SD = 1.69; no guilt conditions: M = 2.02, SD = 1.58.\"",
